// Title: Use Of The SFTP.EXE Binary As A LOLBIN
// Sigma ID: a85ffc3a-e8fd-4040-93bf-78aff284d801
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-11-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1218
// Description: Detects the usage of the "sftp.exe" binary as a LOLBIN by abusing the "-D" flag
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://github.com/LOLBAS-Project/LOLBAS/pull/264
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_lolbin_sftp.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\sftp.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -D .." or ProcessCommandLine contains " -D C:\\")
